{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1149399-drunked-or-drugged-witness","id":1149399,"title":"Drunked or drugged witness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-13T07:12:01-07:00","id":1149399,"title":"Drunked or drugged witness","content":"So, what happens if a Mage tries to use Vulgar Magick in front of drunk sleepers? Or ones under the influence of some drug that makes you trip hard?<br /> <br /> Does it counts as Vulgar with witness regardless? Coincidental because they would just shrug off the magic as something they are seeing under the influence? Or it just depends of the context in the end?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T07:42:12-07:00","id":1149405,"title":"","content":"It would be Vulgar Without Witnesses. Vulgar because a typical observer would reject it. Without witnesses because the drugged out sleeper isn't a typical witness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:33:33-07:00","id":1149430,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It would be Vulgar Without Witnesses.<br /> <br /> I think there's one very specific exception: If you cast a perception altering magic on a Sleeper (like a spell to see the Umbra) it's Vulgar, but it could be Coincidental if the person it's heavily drugged. Same as would happen if you shared perceptions with another mage or a supernatural being. If the drug it's so potent that the guy wouldn't count as Witness, then showing a mental image that only that guy can see wouldn't be Vulgar because the only possible witness it's the one person that doesn't count at Witness (other people can't see you're seeing the Umbra, that's why perception magic it's Coincidental to begin with), and because people &quot;see things&quot; in violent drug trips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:41:39-07:00","id":1149518,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to say that it <b>could be</b> Vulgar without Witnesses. Drugs use impact isn't consistent. Even heavy hallucinogenic drugs don't mean you spend the whole time divorced from reality.<br /> <br /> And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> notes, setting things up can matter a lot. A mage that's convinced a Sleeper to go through the ritual use of drugs to experience a spiritual vision, and then casts some mind/perception altering magic on them, is an exceedingly different situation than hoping that you can throw a fireball in front of a bar full of heavy drunks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T22:40:38-07:00","id":1149602,"title":"","content":"Actually, this brings up an interesting general question...<br /> <br /> Let's presume that a Mage does an effect that is normally vulgar.<br /> Let's presume that there is a single, uninitiated but perhaps gullible witness around.<br /> Let's not dive into specifics, but just say that the Mage does not *visually* window-dress things to hide the vulgarity, but somehow convinces the witness beforehand of the simple blatant..normality of what they are about to do, with simple words.<br /> <br /> Does it become fully coincidental?<br /> <br /> Or, put differently, does the power of a single, normal, non-associated, unaware-of-the-supernatural witness that fully accepts what is happening override the hypothetical observer into full coincidence, if no other actual witnesses are present and the present witness is not intoxicated or otherwise mind-controlled?<br /> <br /> And if (or if not) so, where is the blurry line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-14-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T01:58:44-07:00","id":1149621,"title":"","content":"99.9% of the time: No the real witnesses do not override the hypothetical witnesses to make something coincidental that the hypothetical would consider vulgar..<br /> <br /> The edge case is exactly what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> brought up. Sensory magic is usually coincidental. There's no way for a hypothetical witness to see me give myself the ability to see auras, or see me give that ability to a Sleeper. But this is still usually vulgar because we consider real witnesses as valid for determining vulgarity even if it's all just in their own head. However because it's all in their head, it's a blurry line as to what they might and might not accept compared to a hypothetical subject of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T02:17:38-07:00","id":1149625,"title":"","content":"Another case would be if a reality zone was brought into being during, say, an LSD inthused rave. Pretty sure if you transform into an animal while in a club full of tripping sleepers, they wouldn't even know what happened was impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:00:04-07:00","id":1149781,"title":"","content":"I can remember somewhere in the M20 manual that if you gather like 100 people of a Cult a Ritual can become coincidental. Still the Storyteller has the last word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T17:42:39-07:00","id":1149808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrakeEpsilon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1149399-drunked-or-drugged-witness?p=1149781#post1149781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can remember somewhere in the M20 manual that if you gather like 100 people of a Cult a Ritual can become coincidental. Still the Storyteller has the last word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myes, however an important part also is that not a single disbelieving witness must be present.<br /> <br /> So I guess the 'ranking' seems to be:<br /> <br /> 1 present disbeliever &gt; 100 believers &gt; Hypothetical Observer.<br /> <br /> Above that you only get (Mystery Percentage) of strong believers in an area, at which point the Reality Zone and thus the local consensus changes - the hypothetical observer takes the side of the local believers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-14-2017, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T01:01:36-07:00","id":1149872,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the line is way blurrier than it is said here yet.<br /> <br /> There are more than one examples in M20 where something doesn't have to match the local consensus to make it fully coincidental.<br /> <br /> There is an example for magic shows and film magic as tools to make things coincidental.<br /> Also there is another paragraph that says something like: &quot;... except when you use drugs on your victim beforehand...&quot; I think that was something with mind magic but I'm not sure.<br /> Another example are Forces effects at an on stage pyro show which make them coincidental.<br /> <br /> All those things aren't coincidental because of the local consensus like summoning an angel at the Saint Peter's Square in Vatican City. (Oldest example - best example.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T02:15:35-07:00","id":1149882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1149399-drunked-or-drugged-witness?p=1149872#post1149872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an example for magic shows and film magic as tools to make things coincidental. &lt;snip&gt;<br /> Another example are Forces effects at an on stage pyro show which make them coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mh, actually these are pretty much normal examples of window-dressing normally vulgar magic so it becomes coincidental in the eyes of onlookers. Things like stage magic and movie props have the nature of potentially not changing the visual effect itself, but the circumstances in which it happens, which causes the coincidence.<br /> <br /> However..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also there is another paragraph that says something like: &quot;... except when you use drugs on your victim beforehand...&quot; I think that was something with mind magic but I'm not sure. </div> </div> </div>This is interesting. But yes, I can see how things like...more outrageous hallucinations via Mind-Magick become coincidental if the victim is pretty much aware that they have been drugged - mostly because depending on the drug, that can become quite normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}